## v0.7.7 – Settings Page Enhancements & Onboarding UI Overhaul
**Date:** December 26, 2025, 11:45 PM

### Changes Made:
- Added editable nickname field to settings General tab with save functionality
- Made email, role, and plan display as read-only fields with grey styling
- Moved "Sessions" / "Logout all devices" from General to Privacy & Data tab
- Increased spacing between Privacy & Data sections to 56px for visual hierarchy
- Decreased gap between section descriptions and buttons to 8px
- Added hard page refresh after nickname update to sync header display
- Overhauled onboarding ticket to use new tag/project UI matching card component:
  - Tags stored as array instead of comma-separated string
  - Plus button (circular) to add new tags
  - Individual pill-shaped tag buttons that are clickable to edit
  - Backspace on empty tag input deletes the tag
  - Project shows plus button when empty, blue badge when filled
- Project badge uses blue-50 background and blue-700 text when filled
- Project input auto-sizes to content width (no fixed width stretching)
- Auto-focus project/tag fields when tabbing into them (no click required)
- Tab from project moves to tags, Enter/Tab in tags adds tag and keeps input open
- Unified tooltip background and line colors to grey-900 (#222832)
- Auto-focus title textarea when onboarding card mounts
- Added pointer-events: none to animating-out ticket to prevent ghost cursor

### Backend Changes:
- Extended UpdateProfileRequest struct with optional Name and Email fields
- Updated UpdateProfile handler with email validation and uniqueness check
- Returns 400 for invalid email format, 409 if email already in use

### Current Status:
- Settings page fully functional with editable nickname
- Onboarding flow polished with consistent UI matching the card component
- Keyboard navigation works smoothly through task title, project, and tags
- All changes build successfully on both frontend and backend

### Unresolved Issues:
- None

